          },
          {
            "id": 2542,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<p>As for the animal enclosures and central facilities, the most dramatic changes have occurred in this area. A new wild animals exhibit has been added to the upper left section, while the Australian animals enclosure has remained in approximately the same location on the western side. The birds and chimpanzees exhibits, which previously occupied the lower-left area, have been removed entirely, and this space is now home to the seal show, which has been moved from its original northeastern position. Furthermore, the African animals enclosure has been relocated from the left side to a more central position, where it now occupies a smaller area. Meanwhile, the gift shop has been retained in the center-right but has undergone renovation, and a cable car system has been installed on the eastern side near the picnic area, which has also been preserved.</p>",
